$ satlink net tcp -h
exit status 0
--- stdout
Connect to HOST PORT and relay standard input and output, like netcat

Usage: satlink net tcp [OPTIONS] <HOST> <PORT>

Arguments:
  <HOST>  
  <PORT>  

Options:
  -p, --port <PORT>            Serial device (auto-detected by USB vendor ID when omitted) [env: SATLINK_PORT=]
  -b, --baud <BAUD>            [default: 19200]
      --simulate[=<SIMULATE>]  Use a simulated handset instead of a real one, with Iridium's real timing (the default) or instant responses [possible values: iridium, instant]
  -v, --verbose...             Log what the link is doing (-v), in more detail (-vv, -vvv)
  -h, --help                   Print help (see more with '--help')
--- stderr
